{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":81372,"duration_api_ms":114579,"num_turns":5,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"11502d04-5384-4e31-afb3-92114c82073a","total_cost_usd":0.4374003,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25994,"cache_read_input_tokens":80638,"output_tokens":1596,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25994,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":119,"outputTokens":6935,"cacheReadInputTokens":652448,"cacheCreationInputTokens":75728,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.19469879999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":1596,"cacheReadInputTokens":80638,"cacheCreationInputTokens":25994,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24270150000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments are well-founded and verified against the codebase. Amendment fr-2-7ec97029 addresses confirmed dead-code parameters. Amendment fr-2-b9d261ac identifies the only inconsistently hardcoded Monod K constant. Amendment fr-2-7a74aad7 describes a real, verified bug in the zero-volume startup override path that silently zeroes all dissolved chemistry.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7ec97029","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: all four private helpers (shrimp_feeding, update_condition, update_molt_stress, emit_molt_stress_warning) accept `_volume_l: f64` with an underscore prefix, and none reference it. They all use `state.water_volume_l()` or TankState concentration helpers internally. The caller `step_daily_shrimp` computes `volume_l` once for a zero-check guard but the helpers don't need it. Removing the dead parameter is a clean, low-risk cleanup that prevents confusion and dead-code drift."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b9d261ac","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: line 83 of nitrogen_cycle.rs has `do_total / (do_total + 2.0)` with a comment '// half-sat ~2 mg total'. This is the sole hardcoded Monod K constant in the entire nitrogen cycle module. All other guilds (AOB: aob_k_tan_mg, aob_k_do_mg; NOB: nob_k_nitrite_mg, nob_k_do_mg; Comammox: comammox_k_tan_mg, comammox_k_do_mg) and the decomposer DOC term (decomposer_k_doc_mg) are parameterized in ProcessParams. Extracting this into a `decomposer_k_do_mg` field restores consistency, makes the constant tunable, and eliminates a hidden magic number."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7a74aad7","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified as a real bug. When `source_water_profile_id` is None and only a substrate override is applied, the code calls `rescale_totals_for_volume(old_volume_l, new_volume_l)`. But `old_volume_l` is captured AFTER geometry overrides (including fill_ratio) have already been applied, so it can be near-zero. In `rescale_totals_for_volume`, when `old_volume_l <= f64::EPSILON`, the scale becomes exactly 0.0, zeroing all 17+ dissolved total fields. This produces a physically impossible state: positive water volume with zero chemistry. The repro path is confirmed — low fill_ratio with substrate-only override triggers it. The fix (rebuild from effective source-water profile or special-case 0→positive volume) plus a regression test is the correct approach."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9b9ba069-2c06-4ffc-8e01-55148cad11ae"}
